# Production Ready

## Objective

Shippable quality: no TODO hacks, debug leftovers, or half-finished paths in code that will run in real use.

## Requirements

- No placeholder implementations presented as complete.
- Remove temporary debug logging and commented dead code before finish.
- Use project config systems  -  avoid hardcoded secrets or environment-specific magic values.
- Handle realistic error paths; fail safely.
- Honor project threading/concurrency contracts when defined.

## Definition of Done (general)

- Scope complete per request.
- Verified (see `testing.mdc`).
- Self-reviewed (see `self-review.mdc`).
- Documented when significant (`documentation-first.mdc`).

## Cross-links

`security-first.mdc`, `clean-code.mdc`, `configuration.mdc`.

## Golden Rule

Production-ready means another team could deploy and operate this without rescue edits.